---

<Base
  title={SEO_TITLE}
  description={DESCRIPTION}
  path={PATH}
  ogImage={IMAGE.hero}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
  schema={schema}
  ogType="article"
>
  <article class="rd-guide">
    <header class="rd-hero reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="rd-kicker">2026 US buying guide · Last reviewed 27 September</p>
        <h1>{H1}</h1>
        <p class="rd-standfirst">
          “Robot dog” now describes completely different products: a <strong>$70 toy</strong>, a
          <strong>connected AI pet</strong>, an <strong>open-source coding platform</strong>, a
          <strong>ROS quadruped</strong> or a <strong>soft companion for an older adult</strong>.
          We separate those jobs first, then choose the strongest fit in each.
        </p>
        <div class="rd-hero__badges">
          <span>6 category winners</span>
          <span>Manufacturer sources checked</span>
          <span>Retailer prices dated</span>
          <span>No invented overall score</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rd-byline">
          <span>Research and buying guide by</span><a href={FOUNDER.path}>{FOUNDER.name}</a><span>·</span>
          <a href="/review-methodology/">How BotPlanet researches robots</a>
        </div>
        <div class="rd-actions">
          <a class="rd-button rd-button--primary" href="#comparison">Compare the six picks</a>
          <a class="rd-button" href="#method">See the evidence standard</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="rd-media rd-hero__media">
        <img
          src={IMAGE.hero}
          width="1536"
          height="864"
          alt="Several kinds of robot dog shown together for children, families, programmers and companion use."
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>One search term, five different buying decisions: toy, AI pet, learning platform, advanced quadruped and soft companion.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </header>

    <section class="rd-evidence-hero reveal" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div>
        <p class="rd-kicker">Evidence standard</p>
        <h2 id="method-title">Research-led. Not hands-on tested by BotPlanet.</h2>
        <p>
          We have <strong>not physically tested these six units side by side</strong>, so we do not
          pretend we have. Recommendations come from manufacturer documentation, current retailer
          checks, BotPlanet's existing product research and clear buyer-fit comparisons. A claim
          that cannot be tied to a source is either removed or labelled uncertain.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rd-evidence-grid">
        <article><strong>Manufacturer first</strong><span>Core capability comes from the maker or its technical documentation where available.</span></article>
        <article><strong>Retailer second</strong><span>Prices, coupons, stock and review counts are dated snapshots, never permanent facts.</span></article>
        <article><strong>Variants stay separate</strong><span>A kit with LiDAR is not silently merged with a cheaper kit that does not include it.</span></article>
        <article><strong>No fake precision</strong><span>We removed percentage “fit scores” because a number such as 94/100 meant nothing without a reproducible test.</span></article>
      </div>
      <p class="rd-note">
        This is the standard BotPlanet uses across research-led reviews. <a href="/review-methodology/">Read the full review methodology →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="rd-winners" aria-label="Best robot dog picks by buyer type">
      {winners.map(([label, name, reason, href]) => (
        <a class="rd-winner" href={href}>
          <small>{label}</small><strong>{name}</strong><span>{reason}</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </nav>

    <section class="rd-section reveal">
      <header class="rd-section__head">
        <p class="rd-kicker">The answer first</p>
        <h2>Choose the job before you choose the robot</h2>
        <p>
          This is the most important distinction on the page. A machine can be technically more
          advanced and still be the wrong present.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="rd-intent-cards">
        <a class="rd-intent-card" href="#ruko"><span>Child / easy gift</span><strong>Ruko 18011</strong><small>Immediate play, remote control, gestures and simple programmable actions.</small></a>
